+## v0.1.6 — LG webOS pairing + power-off test
+
+Saved LG devices now have an explicit **Pair LG webOS** action. The phone tries secure WebSocket port 3001 first and falls back to port 3000. First-time pairing shows the normal LG authorization prompt; the returned client key is persisted in the device profile.
+
+After pairing, the app requests `ssap://com.webos.service.connectionmanager/getinfo` and stores any Wi-Fi/Ethernet MAC addresses the TV exposes. **Test Power Off** sends `ssap://system/turnOff`. **Forget LG Pairing** removes only the stored client key. Wake-on-LAN and the v0.1.5 active LAN scanner remain unchanged.
+
+## Device Quick Add / Gesture Mapper (v0.1.6)
 
